note fma_mix: fma rounds once. f64 a = 1 + 2^-30, b = 1 - 2^-30, c = -1 (bit patterns below, from Wolfram;
note groups4.expect): fma a b c is -2^-60 exactly, while mul then add rounds a*b = 1 - 2^-60 to 1 and gives
note +0. f32 with 2^-13: -2^-26 against +0. Output: those four bit patterns, 8 bytes each, little-endian.
global o uchar 32
fn put8 p ulong v ulong to void
for j ulong 8
put o add p j uchar and shr v mul j 8 255
end
end
fn ff a f64 b f64 c f64 to f64
ret fma a b c
end
fn fu a f64 b f64 c f64 to f64
ret add mul a b c
end
fn gf a f32 b f32 c f32 to f32
ret fma a b c
end
fn gu a f32 b f32 c f32 to f32
ret add mul a b c
end
fn main to int
a = bitcast f64 ulong 4607182418804211712
b = bitcast f64 ulong 4607182418791628800
c = bitcast f64 ulong 13830554455654793216
put8 0 bitcast ulong ff a b c
put8 8 bitcast ulong fu a b c
p = bitcast f32 uint 1065354240
q = bitcast f32 uint 1065351168
r = bitcast f32 uint 3212836864
put8 16 ulong bitcast uint gf p q r
put8 24 ulong bitcast uint gu p q r
w = write 1 o 0 32
ret 0
end
